  "@type": "Dataset",
  "name": "Sensible Heat Data (J-OFURO)",
  "description": "Japanese Ocean Flux data sets with Use of Remote sensing Observations (J-OFURO) Constructed sensible heat flux data using remote sensing observations. Available are monthly mean and 1.0 degree by 1.0 degree grid data over about 5 years (1991-1995). Data variable is sensible heat flux (W/m 2 ). Data sources include: J-OFURO-LHF, ECMWF LHT, and ECMWF SHF. Data sets are availabe online for download in three file formats: standard ASCII, netCDF, and gzip at http://dtsv.scc.u-tokai.ac.jp/j-ofuro/J-OFURO_SHF.html or anonymous FTP: dtsv.scc.u-tokai.ac.jp/PUB/J-OFURO/SHF/MON. J-OFURO website - http://dtsv.scc.u-tokai.ac.jp/j-ofuro/\n\nDeposited content: descriptive metadata only; underlying research data are not included.\n\nPurpose: To derive homogenous data with high resolution using analysis and satellite data for obtaining globally-covered fluxes between ocean and atmosphere.",
